Every one is an assertion on the exact prose of `Inconclusive::reason`. My spec says that field
"is never empty and is prose for a human reading an adjudication, not a machine-readable code",
and pins only that the two reasons DIFFER from each other. Both suites assert the exact text
anyway. N-of-N: the spec named the field prose and did not say tests may not assert on it.
Vetoed both directions, and filed.

Worth noting what this demonstrates about the module being built. The two failing sets are
DISJOINT, so `witness::read` calls them SeparateFaults -- and the cause is identical in both
directions. That is precisely why the revised clause 7 forbids either variant from claiming a
cause, and it is the clause claude-sonnet's spec critique forced me to add before dispatch.

